From 03652c06ba893a2121a6d867284c6e14435c553f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:42:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: the CRC, the transport's metadata bits and
 the P010 check written again from their specifications

Four files of the module kept GPL-3.0-or-later for small functional
pieces that came from code whose author does not offer it under
GPL-2.0-or-later. They are written again, by someone who was given only
the public texts and a contract of the interfaces and of the required
behaviour (no earlier implementation), and the files pass to
GPL-2.0-or-later:

- dvbridge_eos.h: dvbridge_eos_crc(), the CRC32 of ETSI GS CCM 001
  V1.1.1 clause 6.3.4, the model of ISO/IEC 13818-1 annex A
  (polynomial 0x04C11DB7, register preset to ones, most significant
  bit first, no reflection, no final XOR).
- dvbridge_source.c: CCM_HELPERS and CCM_END (were PACK_PARITY and
  PACK_END), the bits of the metadata packets in the least significant
  bits of the chroma codes as clause 6.4 places them (6.4.1 order,
  6.4.2 scrambling, 6.4.3 three copies, 6.4.4 several packets), and the
  12-bit YCbCr 4:2:2 codes of a pixel as HDMI carries them in RGB888.
- dvbridge_gl_pack.c: the fragment shader of the end-of-signal frame,
  the same functions over the codes of black.
- dvbridge_dmabuf.c: dvbridge_dmabuf_validate_p010(), from the P010,
  R16, GR1616 and RG1616 definitions of drm_fourcc.h, with the same
  decision.

The same bytes and the same decisions, measured against the files
they replace (the transport on Mesa's zink over lavapipe):

- transport frames: 72 of 72 files the same, among them the 28 of the
  bench of the compute rows (profile 7 FEL in YCbCr, in IPT, at
  step-down level 3, with a GUI drawn over; the profile 5 chart in both
  transports), 24 end-of-signal frames (two with codes of black set by
  hand: an odd luma, Cb other than Cr), the GUI read in place, chroma
  centred horizontally and the converted transport;
- the serializer test of 1.0 RC4: its 255 frames the same; the 250
  with packets marked with EOS the same, and on every packet of them
  the CRC equal to the serializer's and its residue 0;
- the CRC: the check value 0x0376E6E7, and 2 000 000 buffers of random
  length the same as before and as a bitwise model of the definition;
- the P010 check: 4 465 921 descriptors (every field of a valid one
  moved alone over its boundary values at 16 x 14 sizes, and 4 000 000
  random ones from those values), 673 090 of them accepted: the same
  decision for every one.

Six mutations are caught: the CRC preset to 0, the copies of a packet
1024 pixels apart, Cb and Cr of black swapped, a pitch of exactly a
row refused, and the parity of luma bits 11..1 in place of 11..0 (in
the end-of-signal shader, whose functions are the same text as the
transport's; on the test pictures the rows that carry metadata are
black bars, whose luma code is even).

The two files that came from the fork take the header of its other
files (its author's original contributions, offered under
GPL-2.0-or-later); the two of Hades only change their SPDX line.
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_dmabuf.c  | 118 +++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_eos.h     |  50 ++++++++++--
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_gl_pack.c | 125 +++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_source.c  | 111 ++++++++++++++++++++------
 4 files changed, 327 insertions(+), 77 deletions(-)

